I am asking you to read my amendment carefully . 
My group is definitely not about to question the obligatory nature of the system , because that would create unlawful discrimination between Member States and within the European Union itself , although it would not surprise me - and I am not referring to you , Mr Stevenson - that someone who had the gall to reject the Charter of Fundamental Rights in this House today could display equal or greater gall in rejecting the identification of ovine and caprine animals . 
Here we are then : I think we have a regulation , the Commission has made us a reasonable proposal , we have also made a reasonable proposal to the Commission , so let us try to finish this matter this morning without too much damage on either side . 
We support free trade , without a doubt , and we support it as a very clear principle . 
on behalf of the ALDE Group . - ( ES ) Mr President , I would also , on behalf of my group and very formally , like to congratulate the rapporteur David Martin on the excellent quality of the report that he is presenting to the House . 
